codex
The first symbolic attempt exposed a useful semantic gap: K’s prover does not infer that a symbolic string is either empty or has positive length. I’m replacing that guard with the directly exhaustive split `S == ""` / `S =/= ""`, and adding the loop invariant as a second reachability claim so recursive iterations can discharge by circularity.
apply patch
